{"step_index":1282,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:45:34Z","thinking":"**Observing Radius and RDN Values**\n\nObserved that graphs with a radius of 4 consistently have an RDN of at least 6. Initial calculations confirm that radius plus one is less than or equal to the observed RDN. This pattern suggests a potential lower bound for RDN based on the radius value. Now attempting to verify this observation through further analysis, specifically, exploring the edge cases.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport scipy.optimize\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef rdn(G):\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    c = []\\n    for v in nodes:\\n        c.extend([1, 2])\\n    A_ub = []\\n    b_ub = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        row = [0] * (2 * n)\\n        row[2*i] = 1\\n        row[2*i+1] = 1\\n        A_ub.append(row)\\n        b_ub.append(1)\\n    for i, v in enumerate(nodes):\\n        row = [0] * (2 * n)\\n        row[2*i] = -1\\n        row[2*i+1] = -1\\n        for u in G.neighbors(v):\\n            j = nodes.index(u)\\n            row[2*j+1] = -1\\n        A_ub.append(row)\\n        b_ub.append(-1)\\n    res = scipy.optimize.milp(c=np.array(c), integrality=np.ones(2*n),\\n                              bounds=scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1),\\n                              constraints=scipy.optimize.LinearConstraint(np.array(A_ub), -np.inf, np.array(b_ub)))\\n    return int(round(res.fun))\\n\\n# Check all trees of order up to 14\\n# Check if any graph has radius >= 4 and rdn <= 4\\n# Actually, if rdn <= 4, can radius >= 4?\\nfound = False\\nfor n in range(8, 15):\\n    for _ in range(50):\\n        G = nx.random_labeled_tree(n)\\n        if nx.radius(G) >= 4:\\n            r = rdn(G)\\n            if r <= 4:\\n                print('Found tree with rad >= 4 and rdn <= 4!')\\n                found = True\\n                break\\n    if found: break\\n\\nif not found:\\n    print('No tree with rad >= 4 and rdn <= 4!')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Search for rad >= 4 and rdn <= 4\""}}]}
